clean_summary:
Congratulations to @Etched on announcing their first inference system. Early performance demos are promising, and benchmarking is about to begin.

The new system performance benchmark, AA-AgentPerf, measures how many agents a system can run per megawatt of runtime power.

@Etched: "We're coming out of stealth. We've built our first racks after a successful A0 tapeout, over $1 billion in customer contracts, and $800 million raised. Early customer tests show us achieving state-of-the-art throughput, latency, and power efficiency on inference workloads. Our first racks ship this summer."

Kimi K3 weights have been released. Kimi K3 is now the leading open weights model at 57 in the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index.

Moonshot has released the weights of their 2.6T parameter model under the 'Kimi K3 License,' which is labeled as ‘Commercial Use Restricted.’ Restrictions compared to more permissive licenses like MIT or Apache 2.0 include requiring model-as-a-service businesses with more than $20 million in revenue to enter into a separate agreement. Commercial products with over 100 million monthly active users or $20 million in monthly revenue must also display “Kimi K3” in the user interface.

@Kimi_Moonshot has released their technical report with insights into the model’s architecture and training approach. Links to the weights on Hugging Face, the technical report, and further benchmarks are provided.

summary:
Open weights intelligence advanced today with the release of Kimi K3. The gap between the leading proprietary and open weights models is now just 4 points on the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index, the smallest it has been since the GLM-5 release in February
@Kimi_Moonshot's Kimi K3 scores 57 on the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index. Only two labs have higher-scoring models: @AnthropicAI, with Claude Opus 5 at 61 and Claude Fable 5 at 60, and @OpenAI, with GPT-5.6 Sol at 59.
